// Resolution cases that only show up in combination, extracted from the real
// font where they were originally caught. See src/golden.rs.
//
// `badge-a`/`badge-b` are never declared: they are synthesized from the
// `:mono` and `:color` halves, which are themselves declared by a name
// pattern. Looking the halves up under their unexpanded pattern name finds
// nothing, which is how the editor and the built font came to disagree about
// whether `badge-a` exists.

name-parts $ab = a b

glyph badge-($ab):mono 2 2
....
....
ref ok 0 0

glyph badge-($ab):color 2 2
....
....
ref ok 0 0 fill #FF0000

// Forces the color/mono synthesis by referring to the bare name.
remap badge : ok -> badge-a

// Remap operands carry name-part patterns that only the GSUB builder expands.
// Every expansion of this one exists, so it must stay quiet...
remap badge-pattern : ok -> badge-($ab)

// ...while this one expands to glyphs that do not exist. The GSUB builder
// drops such rules silently, so unless resolution expands remap operands the
// same way the builder does, a whole feature can go missing unreported.
remap badge-broken : ok -> no-such-badge-($ab)

feature liga for latn : badge
feature liga for latn : badge-pattern
feature liga for latn : badge-broken

assume unused badge-($ab):mono
assume unused badge-($ab):color
